{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>A threshing-sledge.</b> Known, and like it המוריגי״ם (II Samuel 24:22)." "<b>Sharp.</b> That is, it is decreed according to rule, like כֵּן מִשְׁפָּטֶיךָ אַתָּה חֲרַצְתָּ (I Kings 20:40). Do not marvel because Scripture speaks to Israel in feminine language and also masculine language in one verse, for the feminine refers to the congregation, and it is not literally feminine." "And the sense of <b>you shall thresh mountains</b> is a parable for the Babylonians."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:24.693106940Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}